WEBVTT

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.130
On I go, searching for...

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.330
The past that was stolen from me

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.420
Wandering on through...

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:27.130
This city, so strange to see

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:32.080
Choked by the scent of flames that seems to...

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:33.880
Cling to me

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.630
Didn't we both say our goodbyes...

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.540
And go our separate ways?

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.790
When you see the face of hell...

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.330
It will squeeze your heart dry

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:52.750
Fighting on seems so pointless now

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.540
If this must be my fate...

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.790
Then I'll make my mind up now

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.960
So, please, won't you just leave me be...

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.750
Another day

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:15.250
Oh, will tomorrow hold something new to see?

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:40.750
Months have passed since Uoodo
was consumed in fire.

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:44.040
I've now wandered into civil war-torn Kummen.

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:46.330
Mercenaries.

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:47.960
Front lines.

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:50.630
How appropriate for me.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:55.330
But now I know that she is here as well.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:02.040
Doubts

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:06.670
It has to be her. But why...?

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:43.500
You okay?

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:47.420
I appreciate the help, Captain Kan Yu.

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:49.580
I should thank you.

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:52.630
If you hadn't come along, I'd be dead by now.

00:02:53.630 --> 00:02:57.380
Besides, it let me see
how suspiciously you were acting.

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:12.380
You can't go in.

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:15.420
Are they really interrogating Chirico in there?

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:17.750
Why? I demand a meeting!

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:20.920
We've been ordered not to let anyone in.

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:22.960
By Kan Yu?

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:24.710
By General Gon Nu.

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:26.040
What?

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:27.630
Chirico...

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:29.750
I saw it with my own eyes!

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:31.210
Why, in the middle of combat,

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:35.670
did you nearly kill yourself by opening your
cockpit and exposing yourself to the enemy?

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:37.130
I was playing a hunch.

00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:38.580
A hunch?

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:41.170
I thought doing it would confuse my opponent.

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:44.750
A normal human wouldn't have attacked so easily.

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:49.040
I see... You thought you weren't
dealing with a normal man.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:51.790
That the other pilot was a PS.

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:53.540
Well, was it a PS or not?

00:03:57.960 --> 00:03:59.000
I don't know.

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:01.790
I doubt that.

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:05.500
A hero of the Red Shoulders
doesn't casually risk his life.

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:07.460
You must have learned something.

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:11.500
I don't have any proof.

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:13.920
But I think it's definitely a PS.

00:04:14.830 --> 00:04:18.460
A few months ago,
our losses began to climb unexpectedly.

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:21.170
And it all seems due to one enemy pilot.

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:23.670
These are pictures of him
we got from the battles.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:29.170
That's her.

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:33.500
General, the Veela must have
gotten ahold of the PS!

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:35.500
This could be disastrous!

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:40.500
Which makes Chirico's assistance indispensable.

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:43.380
Is there any way to fight this PS, Chirico?

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:47.250
You must have learned something
in your previous encounters.

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:52.580
Compared with us,
a PS's reflexes are much sharper.

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:54.880
A normal human would have
no chance against them.

00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:58.960
You're saying you haven't found
any weaknesses at all?

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:00.290
Not as yet.

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:06.290
In that case, I'll start getting better armor
and weapons upgrades for our AT forces.

00:05:06.290 --> 00:05:07.170
Forget it.

00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:08.250
What?!

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:10.880
You think operations command won't equip us?

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:15.580
I think adding armor and weapons will only
make our ATs heavier and less maneuverable.

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:17.750
They won't help against a PS.

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:22.000
Well, is there any countermeasure, Chirico?

00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:23.750
None.

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:28.420
If you encounter an obviously superior PS,
all you can do is pull back.

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:30.170
Run away?!

00:05:30.170 --> 00:05:33.420
Do that and you'll be
court-martialed for cowardice!

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:37.920
Calm down, Kan Yu.
He's just being a bit blunt.

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:56.750
Chirico!

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:00.210
Did they do anything to you, Chirico?

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:02.580
So, what happened?

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:06.420
Please, later. I'm starving.
Can I get something to eat?

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:08.210
Right. Gotcha.

00:06:09.130 --> 00:06:11.710
Gotho, do you have a computer?

00:06:12.130 --> 00:06:14.830
Yeah, back in my office on the base.

00:06:14.830 --> 00:06:16.920
It's nothing fancy, mind you.

00:06:17.170 --> 00:06:18.580
Can I use it tonight?

00:06:18.580 --> 00:06:20.380
I want to do something
without anyone spying on me.

00:06:20.830 --> 00:06:22.000
Leave that to me.

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:25.170
Even Kan Yu wouldn't break into my office.

00:06:29.630 --> 00:06:34.170
It's okay. I'll stay with you

00:06:34.170 --> 00:06:38.750
I know she's coming back, but I don't mind

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:43.540
It's okay, baby

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:46.960
I guess I'm just used to it now

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:52.130
You never seem to say much

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:56.670
But we have time till dawn

00:06:56.960 --> 00:06:58.830
So, was it her?

00:06:57.790 --> 00:07:02.710
Once in a while, it's okay to wait

00:06:58.830 --> 00:07:03.210
It had to be. The same woman
I fought in Uoodo, the Phantom Lady.

00:07:02.710 --> 00:07:07.210
I'm feeling kind of sentimental today

00:07:03.670 --> 00:07:07.210
But if she knew who you were,
why'd she try to kill you?

00:07:07.210 --> 00:07:11.500
It's okay, baby

00:07:08.380 --> 00:07:09.580
I don't know.

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:14.500
I loved you once upon a time

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:23.170
You must have some idea.

00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:27.500
Well, well. If it isn't the hero.

00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:30.000
You're Chirico, right?

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.000
Yeah.

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:37.250
The word is you went naked in battle.

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:36.380
It's okay

00:07:36.380 --> 00:07:39.210
I'll do as you ask

00:07:37.250 --> 00:07:38.920
You're well informed.

00:07:39.210 --> 00:07:41.210
Even if she comes

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:40.540
Now listen up!

00:07:40.540 --> 00:07:42.170
What you get off on is your own business!

00:07:42.170 --> 00:07:44.750
But don't pull that crap
when you're fighting with me!

00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:47.540
I don't wanna buy it 'cuz of one idiot in the unit!

00:07:47.540 --> 00:07:50.080
Don't worry.
I don't like fighting with idiots, either.

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:52.080
What?! Let's hear that again!

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:52.960
Back off!

00:07:53.710 --> 00:07:55.880
You want to get busted again?

00:07:56.750 --> 00:07:59.080
He's one of us. Leave him alone.

00:07:59.710 --> 00:08:03.710
Chill out, I'm just teachin' him
the mercenary's code.

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:06.170
Just remember this:

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:09.710
Out there, everyone's ass is on the line!

00:08:14.710 --> 00:08:17.420
That's Kiderra. A real bad-ass.

00:08:17.420 --> 00:08:19.380
The fair-skinned guy is Potaria.

00:08:19.380 --> 00:08:21.750
Two of the best pilots at the Assemble base.

00:08:21.750 --> 00:08:23.080
I believe you.

00:08:23.290 --> 00:08:25.170
Hey! Drinks over here!

00:08:25.170 --> 00:08:26.250
Right, coming.

00:08:27.080 --> 00:08:29.130
There's another ace you'll meet.

00:08:29.130 --> 00:08:31.790
He's sorta stand-offish,
but then he's a Quentman after all.

00:08:31.790 --> 00:08:34.460
The Veela are scared to death of him.

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:39.080
I'd stay on their good side if I were you.

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:50.290
Move it!

00:08:51.790 --> 00:08:53.790
What do you want with this?

00:08:53.790 --> 00:08:55.420
Did you lose it or something?

00:08:55.420 --> 00:08:56.670
Move your foot!

00:08:56.670 --> 00:08:58.880
Or maybe you're trying to lift someone's bag.

00:08:58.880 --> 00:08:59.880
Hey, wait!

00:09:01.710 --> 00:09:03.290
You little...! What're you doing?

00:09:03.290 --> 00:09:05.000
No time to explain! Move!

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:25.250
That guy! He planted it!

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:28.250
Veela!

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:30.330
Get him!

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:35.130
Don't expect me to thank you.

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:38.130
Fine. I wasn't trying to save you.

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:41.500
But I'd feel sorry for my friends
if their bar was blown up.

00:09:49.790 --> 00:09:51.580
Those Veela are scary customers.

00:09:51.580 --> 00:09:54.130
You aren't safe walking down the street anymore!

00:09:54.130 --> 00:09:56.580
What are they fighting, anyway?

00:09:56.580 --> 00:09:58.000
Modern times.

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:02.750
Kummen's poor and the royal government
wants to industrialize.

00:10:02.750 --> 00:10:06.250
But the third prince, Kanjelman,
wants to follow the old gods.

00:10:06.830 --> 00:10:08.170
Kanjelman?

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:10.500
That's what started the civil war.

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:13.330
Five years ago he established
his base in an old, ruined city

00:10:13.330 --> 00:10:17.670
and began fighting to establish
the Holy Kingdom of Kummen.

00:10:17.830 --> 00:10:20.170
God has quite a bit of pull with the locals.

00:10:20.500 --> 00:10:25.880
The prince has nearly as much
influence as the government.

00:10:25.880 --> 00:10:28.580
But the military backs the government, right?

00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:30.790
They're unreliable.

00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:33.210
Their main military power
comes from the mercenaries.

00:10:33.210 --> 00:10:36.880
Well, at least that puts food on our tables.

00:10:37.790 --> 00:10:39.790
This isn't just any civil war.

00:10:39.790 --> 00:10:40.960
Why not?

00:10:41.210 --> 00:10:42.460
Because she's here.

00:10:42.460 --> 00:10:46.380
I'm not surprised the Secret Society's
mixed up with the Veela.

00:10:55.210 --> 00:11:00.000
That society being involved
could affect my business.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.380
You'll only get richer and richer, old man.

00:11:02.920 --> 00:11:05.000
I didn't mean that.

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:06.750
Will this thing be enough for you?

00:11:06.750 --> 00:11:09.170
Yeah, it's fine. I'll need it till morning.

00:11:09.170 --> 00:11:10.630
What are you doing exactly?

00:11:10.630 --> 00:11:15.040
This is what controls an AT.
Everyone's is exactly the same.

00:11:15.630 --> 00:11:19.330
It's preprogrammed with
every type of tactical pattern.

00:11:19.540 --> 00:11:23.000
But a ready-made disk like this
is no use against a PS.

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:25.210
I have to customize the memory.

00:11:25.540 --> 00:11:26.880
I see.

00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:30.380
So only you can fight the Phantom Lady.

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:32.380
Well, that's one way to put it.

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:42.920
Chirico's still hiding something about the PS.

00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:44.330
I know he is.

00:11:44.330 --> 00:11:47.170
Then why did you give him
such a light interrogation?

00:11:47.460 --> 00:11:48.830
Calm down, Kan Yu.

00:11:48.830 --> 00:11:53.170
If you keep sending Chirico out onto
the front line to fight the Veela,

00:11:53.170 --> 00:11:55.830
he'll face the PS whether he wants to or not.

00:11:55.830 --> 00:12:00.170
If he keeps risking his life,
his luck'll run out eventually.

00:12:01.080 --> 00:12:02.460
I see...

00:13:09.380 --> 00:13:11.540
Right, I'm coming.

00:13:11.960 --> 00:13:14.080
What do you want at this hour?

00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:15.790
Is Chirico in there, sir?

00:13:15.790 --> 00:13:17.250
Yeah, he is. Why?

00:13:18.130 --> 00:13:19.630
Sortie orders.

00:13:19.630 --> 00:13:22.000
Tell him to report for duty in five minutes.

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:23.130
Excuse me.

00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:25.790
Chirico-

00:13:25.790 --> 00:13:26.670
I heard.

00:13:26.670 --> 00:13:28.670
Kinda sudden. Did you know about this?

00:13:28.670 --> 00:13:29.500
No.

00:13:30.420 --> 00:13:32.960
Watch it. Kan Yu's up to something.

00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:34.040
I'm sure.

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:35.290
You finished?

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:37.750
No. But this should be some help.

00:13:47.040 --> 00:13:48.040
You're late!

00:13:48.040 --> 00:13:49.420
Excuse me, sir.

00:13:49.420 --> 00:13:51.540
I'll give you the mission details later.

00:13:51.540 --> 00:13:53.210
For now you can just introduce yourselves.

00:13:54.420 --> 00:13:56.130
Chirico Cuvie.

00:13:56.130 --> 00:13:57.830
Pol Potaria. How do you do?

00:13:57.830 --> 00:14:01.460
Bully Kiderra. Don't get naked on us, all right?

00:14:02.290 --> 00:14:03.630
Ru Shako.

00:14:05.420 --> 00:14:08.790
You've never seen a Quentman before, have you?

00:14:08.790 --> 00:14:10.040
Uh...

00:14:10.040 --> 00:14:11.380
How do you do?

00:14:11.380 --> 00:14:12.710
Move out!

00:14:44.130 --> 00:14:48.500
This operation may seem unexpected,
but that was due to the need for security.

00:14:49.130 --> 00:14:53.080
We're receiving replacement ATs
from the Kummen government.

00:14:53.630 --> 00:14:58.080
Our mission is to escort them safely
to a front line base.

00:14:58.670 --> 00:14:59.790
Understood?

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:00.580
Roger!

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:03.080
I'm giving you our route. Switch to visual.

00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:06.000
Any questions?

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:06.960
Yes, sir.

00:15:06.960 --> 00:15:07.880
What?

00:15:07.880 --> 00:15:12.130
Escort duty's old hat for us,
but Chirico's still a newbie.

00:15:13.170 --> 00:15:15.630
There are more qualified guys for this
than him, aren't there?

00:15:16.170 --> 00:15:19.000
We may need a specialist.

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:20.500
Isn't that right, Chirico?

00:15:22.380 --> 00:15:23.830
What's that supposed to mean?

00:15:34.670 --> 00:15:37.080
We're going down! Prep for landing.

00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:39.920
All right!

00:15:40.170 --> 00:15:41.500
All right!

00:15:42.130 --> 00:15:43.290
Stop!

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:46.710
Careful! Those things are valuable!

00:15:48.170 --> 00:15:49.380
God damned...!

00:15:51.830 --> 00:15:53.830
Captain Kan Yu! Welcome, sir!

00:15:54.790 --> 00:15:57.210
Big load, isn't it?
How many have you got there?

00:15:57.210 --> 00:16:00.630
Eight units, along with spare parts.

00:16:00.880 --> 00:16:04.670
Those government cowards get to hide
while we risk our asses!

00:16:04.830 --> 00:16:06.790
I want to be at Lake Calday by noon!

00:16:06.790 --> 00:16:08.500
I have some new intelligence, sir.

00:16:09.040 --> 00:16:12.540
We've picked up Veela activity in
Calday sector since last night.

00:16:13.210 --> 00:16:15.210
They know about the operation?

00:16:15.790 --> 00:16:16.790
Move out!

00:16:34.540 --> 00:16:35.500
Chirico!

00:16:36.040 --> 00:16:36.920
What?

00:16:36.920 --> 00:16:39.580
Even if the enemy shows up,
don't do anything stupid.

00:16:39.580 --> 00:16:41.380
I don't wanna waste the only life I've got.

00:16:41.380 --> 00:16:43.170
Neither do I.

00:16:43.170 --> 00:16:46.630
So don't do anything stupid like
hanging onto a bag with a bomb in it.

00:16:48.420 --> 00:16:50.210
Bite me, pal!

00:16:50.210 --> 00:16:51.960
He won that round, Kiderra.

00:16:52.250 --> 00:16:54.130
This isn't a damned picnic!

00:16:54.130 --> 00:16:56.170
No chatter unless it's an emergency!

00:16:56.170 --> 00:16:57.170
Yes, sir!

00:17:15.830 --> 00:17:19.330
Damn, this is irritating. Can't we go any faster?

00:17:23.210 --> 00:17:24.170
What's wrong?

00:17:24.170 --> 00:17:26.880
500 meters, northeast. Something just moved.

00:17:26.880 --> 00:17:28.670
Look sharp, people!

00:17:29.170 --> 00:17:30.290
I don't see anything.

00:17:31.170 --> 00:17:32.580
Nothing on my end.

00:17:32.710 --> 00:17:33.790
Or mine.

00:17:34.040 --> 00:17:35.920
Was it your imagination, Shako?

00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:38.040
It tripped my warning light.

00:17:38.040 --> 00:17:40.250
I know my machine, sir.

00:17:40.250 --> 00:17:44.290
Radar with Quentian metal is never wrong, sir.

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:48.170
I know. But that means
we have to flush out that enemy.

00:17:48.170 --> 00:17:49.170
Let's go!

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:56.420
Do we attack?

00:17:56.420 --> 00:17:58.630
Wait. Let 'em swim a little more.

00:17:59.080 --> 00:18:01.290
Prepare to move to point three.

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:34.250
Forget it. We're stuck.

00:18:34.250 --> 00:18:35.420
What's wrong?

00:18:35.420 --> 00:18:37.460
Can't move. We hit a sand bar.

00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:38.670
Can you back off of it?

00:18:38.670 --> 00:18:40.130
We'll try, sir!

00:18:42.290 --> 00:18:43.500
It won't budge.

00:18:43.500 --> 00:18:44.500
Try full engines, ahead.

00:18:44.500 --> 00:18:45.710
Yes, sir!

00:18:46.210 --> 00:18:47.710
It's not working.

00:18:48.540 --> 00:18:50.330
That's all we need.

00:18:50.330 --> 00:18:52.330
Okay, someone has to dive down
and blow the riverbed.

00:18:52.330 --> 00:18:54.040
That'll be too noisy.

00:18:54.040 --> 00:18:56.250
We'll have to winch it off.

00:18:56.580 --> 00:18:58.290
We can use that rock there.

00:18:58.290 --> 00:19:00.790
Right. Chirico, you go!

00:19:23.380 --> 00:19:26.080
If they attack now, we'll be helpless.

00:19:27.460 --> 00:19:28.500
All set.

00:19:28.500 --> 00:19:29.420
Stop!

00:19:29.830 --> 00:19:31.330
Wind it in!

00:19:53.330 --> 00:19:54.040
Guerillas!

00:19:58.210 --> 00:20:00.710
Here they come! Keep 'em away from the boat!

00:20:23.960 --> 00:20:25.670
Way to go, Shako!

00:20:41.290 --> 00:20:42.460
Keep 'em back!

00:20:53.500 --> 00:20:54.500
There she is!

00:20:59.540 --> 00:21:00.380
Fyana!

00:21:08.080 --> 00:21:10.880
Fyana! It's me! Don't you recognize me?

00:21:22.250 --> 00:21:23.170
Get 'em!

00:21:25.500 --> 00:21:26.540
Potaria!

00:21:27.750 --> 00:21:29.710
Captain, they got Potaria!

00:21:29.710 --> 00:21:30.750
Son of a...!

00:21:31.830 --> 00:21:34.210
Chirico! Cut around from behind!

00:21:34.210 --> 00:21:36.830
I can't! I'm fighting with that blue AT!

00:21:36.830 --> 00:21:37.710
You're what?!

00:21:39.420 --> 00:21:40.380
I've got you!

00:22:17.630 --> 00:22:19.580
Potaria! You still alive?

00:22:19.580 --> 00:22:21.460
Yeah, I guess so.

00:22:31.960 --> 00:22:35.290
My anti-PS program had worked.

00:22:35.920 --> 00:22:38.250
A little more work and we'd be evenly matched.

00:22:40.580 --> 00:22:42.920
She must know it's me.

00:22:43.460 --> 00:22:45.210
But then why is she doing this?

00:22:54.290 --> 00:22:55.710
Next Episode

00:22:55.960 --> 00:22:58.920
The cylinder spins, the hammer cocks back.

00:22:58.920 --> 00:23:01.380
A finger tightens as the trigger is pulled.

00:23:01.380 --> 00:23:06.460
The firing pin makes a sickening click as it
mockingly thrusts into an empty chamber.

00:23:06.460 --> 00:23:10.290
And with a gasp, body and soul tremble in relief.

00:23:10.830 --> 00:23:12.500
Russian roulette.

00:23:12.790 --> 00:23:16.960
Does this most dangerous of games
suit this world?

00:23:17.710 --> 00:23:19.750
Next time, "Clean Sweep"

00:23:19.920 --> 00:23:24.290
Clean Sweep

00:23:19.920 --> 00:23:24.290
Next Time

00:23:20.080 --> 00:23:22.580
With each spin of the cylinder, the danger grows.

00:23:42.540 --> 00:23:46.000
Whenever I'm feeling lonely

00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:49.540
Whenever I'm feeling sad

00:23:49.540 --> 00:23:55.920
I can always see you floating in my mind

00:23:56.420 --> 00:23:59.960
Whenever I'm alone

00:23:59.960 --> 00:24:03.380
Whenever I long for you

00:24:03.380 --> 00:24:09.630
I can always feel you inside my heart

00:24:09.630 --> 00:24:13.130
No matter how far apart we may go

00:24:13.130 --> 00:24:16.540
No matter if my path should part from yours

00:24:16.710 --> 00:24:23.040
The memories of you seem to shine inside my heart...

00:24:23.420 --> 00:24:29.380
Brighter than any other light...
